OL,3,GNEWSAFootball match stopped over
OL,4,Aalleged homophobic abuse
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn a statement, Clay Cross Town
OL,7,Fchairman Lee Watson said one of their
OL,8,Fplayers reported the alleged homophobic
OL,9,Flanguage to the referee. The official
OL,10,Fthen took the players off the field and
OL,11,Fspoke to both managers.
OL,13,FWatson said: "The decision was made by
OL,14,Fthe referee to abandon the fixture
OL,15,Fgiven the alleged comment made by the
OL,16,Fopposition and threats of a violent
OL,17,Fnature."
